      "side": 0,
      "message": "Adding the new host event requires this change, since it requires setting the bit in the upper 32 bits:\n\n```\n\tEC_HOST_EVENT_INVALID \u003d 32,\n\n\t/* Body detect (lap/desk) change event */\n\tEC_HOST_EVENT_BODY_DETECT_CHANGE \u003d 33,\n```\n\n```\n23-02-15 15:50:30.917 ec:~$ bodydetectmode on\n23-02-15 15:50:32.598 [13207.338000 bod![13207.339800 event clear 0x0000000100000000]\n23-02-15 15:50:32.604 ![13207.342900 ACPI query \u003d 33]\n23-02-15 15:50:32.607 y detect mode enabled]\n23-02-15 15:50:32.607 [13207.338700 event set 0x0000000100000000]\n23-02-15 15:50:32.612 [13207.346800 Thermal: Laptop mode]\n```\n\nThe `0x0000000100000000` values is the bitmask with the 33rd bit set.\n\n----\n\nJust to clarify what you\u0027re describing, this should be broken up into 4 CLs total:\n\n1. Remove the `ifdef` check and increase `CONFIG_HOST_EVENT_REPORT_MASK` to the 64b value.\n2. Remove `CONFIG_HOST_EVENT64` (the majority of this patch).\n3. Add `EC_HOST_EVENT_MAX_EVENTS \u003d 65`, use it instead of magic numbers.\n4. Add `EC_HOST_EVENT_BODY_DETECT_CHANGE`",
